    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="15" relname="span">I agree with what you said about the guidelines that are given for website design are from the perspective of what has worked so far.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="3" relname="volitional-cause">I have had to create a few websites in the past</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="22" relname="span">and each time I always do some sort of research just to get an idea of the do's and don'ts</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="21" relname="span">but never have I found an article or a website, that discussed design issues,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="circumstance">where they talked about the general principles of good design and usability that are enlisted in our text.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="23" relname="span">in fact, I was not aware of most of these principles</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="6" relname="circumstance">until I started taking this class.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="24" relname="span">What you will usually find are discussions about what color scheme one should use or how a site should be layed out.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="10" relname="antithesis">It's always 'don't re-invent the wheel' which is good to know</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="19" relname="span">but often times the "wheels" that are being reused don't function as well as they should.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="25" relname="span">When you start to apply the general principles of good design and usability such as ease of use, learnability, and efficiency</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="11" relname="purpose">you will start to see just what a well designed website really looks like.</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="26" relname="span">I myself will always apply these principles</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="13" relname="circumstance">whenever I have to create any web or windows based applications in the future.</segment>
        <group id="15" type="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="1" relname="evidence"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="27" relname="span"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="8" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="18" relname="span"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="20" relname="span"/>
        <group id="22" type="span" parent="21" relname="concession"/>
        <group id="23" type="span" parent="20" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="24" type="span" parent="18" relname="evidence"/>
        <group id="25" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="26" type="span" parent="25" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="27" type="span" parent="17" relname="antithesis"/>
    </body>
